Z||000000||Dave85||10-23-1999||09:39 PM||||<BR>I was on my way home tonight and this Mustang 5.0 pulled up next to me and is gassing his car, wanting to run. This thing was LOUD!!! It took a couple of lights to get the chance and I could tell his clutch was shot. So, there we are, the light turns and I let off the brake and was gone. I left him a car length and a half and he never gained any! I guess he didn't have any low end torque due to that exhaust.  The guy pulled off the road first chance he got.     ||||reg||1
Z||000001||TOM||10-23-1999||09:41 PM||||Wat to go. I did the same to a mid eighties t-bird the other day. He didnt turn off but he could never catch me. At the next light he wouldnt even look over my way. Hmmm I wonder why?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shaun41178||10-23-1999||10:50 PM||||Good Kill Dave.<P>List your mods and year/model.<P>You said you lifted off the brake so I am guessing you have an auto tranny?<P>Great kill again||||reg||1
Z||000003||turbo86se||10-23-1999||11:49 PM||||Good going Dave, last year the same thing happened to me, I was sitting at a red light when a big, ugly Mustang GT pulled up next to me. The guy driving the Mustang was looking at me and revving his engine. I was driving my automatic 88 coupe. This was a wide left turn only, and when the light turned green, we both took off. The Fiero hugged that turn like it was on rails. I noticed in my side- view mirror, the Mustang was all over the road! I hit the speed limit and backed off with a good four car-lengths ahead of the Mustang. He finally caught up and roared past me. I just laughed!!<BR>Fiero is stock except for K&N filter, straight pipe in place of cat., and a good tune up!<P>||||reg||10
